course: dictionary
lesson: 10517
title: Old money: twopence
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Twopence is an old British word for two pennies. Look at the clue in this sentence: «giving a porter twopence to keep a strict eye on him». You pay a porter with money, and twopence is a small amount, so it must mean two pennies. Swap in two pennies and the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Twopence can also be written tuppence, and the two words mean the same thing. Before 1971 there was a British coin called twopence, worth two old pennies. Today the 2p coin is its modern version.
explain: Words can also be used in phrases. «I do not care twopence» means I do not care at all. The clue is the word care: a tiny amount of money stands for a tiny amount of caring.
fact: Twopence means two pennies in British money.
fact: Tuppence is another spelling of twopence, and it means the same thing.
fact: Before 1971 there was a British coin called twopence, worth two old pennies.
fact: Before 1971 there were 12 pennies in a shilling and 240 pennies in a pound.
fact: «Not care twopence» is an informal phrase meaning to not care at all.
exercise: «giving a porter twopence to keep a strict eye on him» What is twopence here? | A bag of crumbs | A large sum, like a pound | A type of railway ticket | *Two pennies, a very small amount of money
exercise: Someone says, «I don't care twopence about the game.» What does this mean? | *They do not care at all | They care about two games | They will pay two pennies to watch | They care very much and want to win
exercise: A twopence coin before 1971 was worth how much? | Two pounds | *Two old pennies | Two shillings | Twelve pennies
test: In old money, how many pennies were in a pound? | *240 | 100 | 1000 | 12
test: Which word is another name for twopence? | Pound | Shilling | Penny | *Tuppence
exam: Which sentence uses twopence to mean not caring at all? | «A bag of crumbs cost twopence.» | *«I do not care twopence what you think.» | «She counted her twopence carefully.» | «The coin was worth twopence before 1971.»
